Automatic Electric Fence Power Failure Alert System

&nbsp;

## 1\. Statement

&nbsp;

In farming, electric fencing is commonly used to protect crops from animals. However, when the power supply fails at night, the fence becomes inactive and the farmer may not notice the failure. This project detects the loss of power in the electric fence and immediately gives an audible buzzer alert.

## 2\. Materials Required

&nbsp;

Arduino Uno

LDR Sensor Module

Buzzer

LED

Resistors

Breadboard

Jumper wires

Battery / power supply

Electric fencing setup

Connecting wires

## 3\. Procedure

&nbsp;

Connect the LDR sensor module to the Arduino Uno.

Connect the buzzer and LED to the Arduino as output indicators.

Power the monitoring circuit using a suitable battery.

Position the sensor to monitor the fence power/status indicator.

Program the Arduino to detect the normal and power-failure conditions.

When the fence power is available, the system remains in normal monitoring mode.

When the fence power fails, the Arduino activates the buzzer and LED to alert the farmer.

## 4\. Notes

&nbsp;

The system provides a simple 24-hour fence power-failure alert.

It helps farmers identify power failure quickly, especially at night.

The project improves crop protection by reducing the time during which the fence remains inactive.

The monitoring circuit should be electrically isolated from the high-voltage fence.

